/* src/core/axes.def — [REVW.4] wave 4 (D111, L1-X9): THE SINGLE SOURCE OF
 * THE OPTIMIZATION-AXIS TABLE — each axis's option bit, its CLI spelling(s)
 * and its default polarity, in one place, with every reader derived from it.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The 2026-09-17 code review found this table kept in
 * THREE hand-maintained sources reconciled by TWO awk scrapers:
 * `cli_parse`'s twenty-two `strcmp` arms (`cli/main.c`), the `DENY_NAMES`
 * value->symbol table and the `cli_flag_of` (axis, candidate) ladder in
 * `src/dump/axes_dump.c`, and the fifteen hand-typed `cli_flag` strings in
 * `emit_predicate_axes` — with `tests/registry/axes_registry_check.sh` and
 * `tests/axes/run_axes.sh` each running its OWN `awk` pass over
 * `cli/main.c`'s TEXT to check the first two against each other. Frank ruled
 * it built (D111, "Yes. I like single source"). The A3 cost INVERTS here:
 * the two scrapers are DELETED rather than re-aimed, because a check that
 * reconciles three sources has nothing left to reconcile once there is one.
 *
 * WHAT THIS TABLE IS NOT. It is NOT the home of the option BIT VALUES.
 * Those live where they are a CONTRACT — `lib/pcrec.h`'s own enum, the only
 * public header — and a row below names the macro as a TOKEN, so the bit is
 * spelled exactly once in this tree and this file holds no copy of it to
 * drift from. (`limits.def`'s rows may likewise reference an earlier row's
 * own name.) That is why the ship-shape question D111 left open — whether
 * `lib/pcrec.h`'s enumeration should become a generated block — does not
 * arise: there is no duplication to generate away. See
 * `docs/dev/lanes/w4_report.md` item 4 for the measured cost of the
 * generated-block alternative and why this one is smaller in every column.
 *
 * THE ROW SHAPE, one line per AXIS:
 *
 *   PCREC_AXIS(deny_macro, deny_flag, force_macro, force_flag, default_state)
 *
 *   deny_macro    the `lib/pcrec.h` bit that DENIES this axis, as a token,
 *                 or `0` if the axis has no denial. The X-macro stringifies
 *                 it where a symbol NAME is wanted (`#deny_macro`), so the
 *                 printed name and the value used cannot drift apart — the
 *                 trick `axes_dump.c`'s own `V()` macro already used, now
 *                 applied once instead of per call site.
 *   deny_flag     the CLI spelling that sets it ("-fno-X"), or "" when
 *                 there is no deny macro.
 *   force_macro   the bit that FORCES this axis on, as a token, or `0`.
 *                 Two axes have one today (`prefilter`, `prefilter-collapse`
 *                 — lib/pcrec.h explains why each is a pair rather than a
 *                 deny-only flag).
 *   force_flag    its CLI spelling ("-fX"), or "".
 *   default_state PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON — the optimization runs unless
 *                 denied, which is every row today — or
 *                 PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_OFF, an axis a build does NOT take
 *                 unless asked. The column exists because the shape has to
 *                 admit an OFF-by-default axis without changing: it is
 *                 carried for [EMIT-VERB]'s coming `-fcomments` row (default
 *                 OFF, Frank's ruling 2026-09-19), which is a row and not a
 *                 special case. NOTHING READS IT YET, and it is here rather
 *                 than added later on purpose — a column added with its
 *                 first consumer is a column every existing row has to be
 *                 revisited for.
 *
 * WHAT IS NOT A ROW, and each has a reason rather than an omission:
 *   - `PCREC_CASELESS`, `PCREC_EMIT_MAIN`, `PCREC_NO_CAPTURES`,
 *     `PCREC_TRACE` — SEMANTIC flags, not optimization axes. They change
 *     what the artifact MEANS or REPORTS, not which of two answer-identical
 *     shapes it takes, and none is spelled `-f`.
 *   - `--engine=`, `--unroll=K`, `--vm-entry-shape=N`, `--tune=N` — VALUE
 *     parameters, not `pcrec_options.flags` bits. `--engine=` is
 *     additionally DO-OR-DIE (it refuses rather than selecting), which is a
 *     different contract from a denial.
 *   - `--fno-step-budget` — spelled with two dashes and setting a VALUE
 *     (`PCREC_STEP_BUDGET_NONE`), not a flag bit.
 *
 * READERS TODAY, all derived, none hand-typed:
 *   cli/main.c          `cli_axis_apply` — the whole `-f`/`-fno-` grammar
 *   src/dump/axes_dump.c `pcrec_axis_macro_name`/`pcrec_axis_cli_flag` —
 *                       the `--list-axes` dump's deny/force macro-name,
 *                       deny/force bit-number and `cli_flag` columns
 * and, through that dump rather than through this file,
 *   tests/axes/run_axes.sh          the answer-identity sweep's axis list
 *   tests/registry/axes_registry_check.sh   the registry check
 *
 * The bits are deliberately NOT in bit order below: the rows are grouped by
 * FAMILY the way `lib/pcrec.h`'s own prose groups them, because that is the
 * order a reader looking for "the VM's rung ladder" or "the DFA scan's
 * axes" needs, and bit order is recoverable from the macro. */

#ifndef PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON
#define PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON  1
#define PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_OFF 0
#define PCREC_AXIS_DEF_UNDEF 1
#endif

/* ---- the VM's rung ladder ([ENG-BREP], D47.3) -------------------------
 * Each is DENY-ONLY and composes PER QUANTIFIER: a quantifier walks its own
 * ladder skipping the denied rungs, so a denial needs no way to ADDRESS one
 * quantifier inside a pattern. A strategy that cannot be denied cannot be
 * differentially tested, which is why every one of these exists. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_POSSESSIFY,   "-fno-possessify",   0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_REVDET,       "-fno-revdet",       0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_COUNTER,      "-fno-counter",      0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_LENGTH_PRUNE, "-fno-length-prune", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- axes that can change WHICH ENGINE a pattern gets ------------------
 * Both leave a construct in the tree that is DFA-excluding, so denying one
 * can move `RX_ENGINE` to "vm" and `--engine=dfa` plus the denial can
 * REFUSE. See lib/pcrec.h at each macro. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_ATOMIC_DISCHARGE, "-fno-atomic-discharge", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_SPLICE_CALLS,     "-fno-splice-calls",     0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- the two FORCE PAIRS, and they are pairs for two different reasons -
 * `prefilter` is one verdict for the WHOLE artifact rather than a
 * per-quantifier ladder step, so there is something to force; forcing it on
 * a pure-DFA-selected pattern is DO-OR-DIE and refuses (asserted in
 * src/opt/select_engine.c, not in the parser). `prefilter-collapse` decides
 * WHICH LANGUAGE the prefilter's DFA recognises, and forcing it is NOT
 * do-or-die — the collapsed language of a pattern with nothing to collapse
 * IS its exact language, so there is nothing to refuse. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_PREFILTER, "-fno-prefilter",
           PCREC_FORCE_PREFILTER, "-fprefilter", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_PREFILTER_COLLAPSE, "-fno-prefilter-collapse",
           PCREC_FORCE_PREFILTER_COLLAPSE, "-fprefilter-collapse", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- AST-level rewrites ([OPT-ALTCLS], [ENG-ISL], [FORM-CHAR]) ---------
 * Deny-only for the rung ladder's reason: each qualifying site is its own
 * selection point, addressed independently. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_ALTCLS_MERGE,  "-fno-altcls-merge",  0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_ALTCLS_FACTOR, "-fno-altcls-factor", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_ALT_ISLAND,    "-fno-alt-island",    0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_CLS_FOLD,      "-fno-cls-fold",      0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- emitted-shape axes: the VM entry chain and the unroll ladder ------ */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_TIERED_ENTRY, "-fno-tiered-entry", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_SIZE_TERM,    "-fno-size-term",    0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- the DFA scan's own axes ([OPT-3], [OPT-K], [ENG-ABS], [OPT-5]) ----
 * These five are the ones `--list-axes` reports on its `list`-kind rows,
 * where the deny bit comes straight off `src/gen/emit_dfa.c`'s own live
 * candidate arrays rather than from a hand-written row. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_PREMUL_TABLE, "-fno-premul-table", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_OFFSET_SKIP,  "-fno-offset-skip",  0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_ANCHORED_DFA, "-fno-anchored-dfa", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_SCAN_EDGE,    "-fno-scan-edge",    0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_START_PINNED, "-fno-start-pinned", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- the one axis that is NOT answer-identical ([K50]) -----------------
 * Both settings describe a real semantics for a mid-character caller
 * startpos, so which one an artifact carries is a CONTRACT fact rather than
 * a shape choice — the reason it is the only member not masked out of
 * `rx_info.flags`. It is a row here all the same: what this table holds is
 * the SPELLING and the BIT, and those are the same kind of fact either way. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_STARTPOS_GUARD, "-fno-startpos-guard", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- the whole-window PRE-CHECKS ([OPTLOOP.1] batch 1, D119) -----------
 * Facts about the WHOLE pattern, derived from the AST above either engine,
 * that let a search answer NOMATCH or narrow its start range before any
 * attempt runs. Deny-only: each is one artifact-level verdict, so there is
 * nothing to address inside a pattern and nothing to force — the analysis
 * either proves the fact or does not, and a forced build could only ask it
 * to emit a bound it has not proved. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_VM_ANCHOR_BOUND, "-fno-vm-anchor-bound", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_END_WINDOW, "-fno-end-window", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_REQ_BYTE, "-fno-req-byte", 0, "", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON)

/* ---- the emitted artifact's human commentary ([EMIT-VERB], D112) -------
 * The first row whose axis is not an OPTIMIZATION at all: it changes no
 * emitted CODE, only whether the prose around it is written. It is a FORCE
 * PAIR for a reason no other pair here has — the axis is OFF by default, so
 * the force flag restores rather than pins, and the deny flag exists so a
 * command line can override a `config`/target block that turned it on.
 * `default_state` below is this column's first reader; see lib/pcrec.h at
 * both macros and docs/spec/tuning.md §2.24. */
PCREC_AXIS(PCREC_NO_COMMENTS, "-fno-comments",
           PCREC_FORCE_COMMENTS, "-fcomments", PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_OFF)

#undef PCREC_AXIS
#ifdef PCREC_AXIS_DEF_UNDEF
#undef PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_ON
#undef PCREC_AXIS_DEFAULT_OFF
#undef PCREC_AXIS_DEF_UNDEF
#endif
